# Do-not-touch: protected core

## Context

`app/src/store.ts` (the dispatch/notify engine) and `app/src/types.ts` (the
`AppState`/`Action` contract) are load-bearing — every other file depends on
their shape. Changing them ripples through the whole app.

## Rule

- Do NOT edit `app/src/store.ts` or `app/src/types.ts` unless the user has
  explicitly asked to change one of those two files by name in the current
  request.
- Normal feature work (new actions, new behavior) extends
  `app/src/reducer.ts` and `app/src/actions.ts`, not the protected files.
- If a task seems to require touching `store.ts` or `types.ts`, stop and ask
  the user for explicit confirmation before editing, explaining why it's
  needed.

## How to verify

1. `git diff --stat -- app/src/store.ts app/src/types.ts` (or diff against the
   last known-good commit) — empty, unless the user explicitly requested the
   change in this session.
2. Re-read the conversation/task description: does it name `store.ts` or
   `types.ts` directly? If not, any diff to those files is a violation.
